      "document_date": "2026-11-20",
      "accessed": "2026-11-20",
      "section": null,
      "note": "Emailed reply (county-wide, not township-specific): an owner may tent camp overnight on vacant private land with no county permit, minimum lot size or annual day limit, and may return over multiple years without building a house; a seasonal platform yurt is OK; any structure 200 sq ft or larger needs a county building permit, and electrical, mechanical or plumbing work needs its own permits; toilet and wastewater questions go to the health department; not aware of separate camping ordinances but advised checking township rules and deed restrictions."
